# The build context is the repo root, which is a large Android project. Everything below is
# excluded before the context is uploaded to the daemon, so the build stays fast and — the part
# that matters — no credential ever reaches an image layer.
#
# ⚠️ **This file lives at the repo root and not beside the Dockerfile, deliberately.** BuildKit
# does support a per-Dockerfile `tools/web/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, but it is the newer form and
# an older or differently-configured builder ignores it silently — at which point the exclusions
# below stop applying and `secrets/` goes into the build context. An ignore file that might not
# be read is worse than none, because it looks like protection. The context root is where every
# builder looks.

# ⚠️ Secrets first, and never negated below. `*.local.properties` holds the Nextcloud app
# password; `secrets/` holds the container's. Neither belongs in a build context at all: a file
# copied into a layer stays in that layer even if a later step deletes it.
*.local.properties
secrets/
.env
.env.*

# The Android build, which is most of the repository by size and none of it by relevance.
build/
*/build/
**/build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
android/
app/
core/
build-logic/
gradle/
*.jar
*.aar
*.apk

# Working data. `recordings-pulled/` is a real 12 MB lecture used as a test fixture.
recordings-pulled/
graphify-out/
.claude-flow/
tools/web/.cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Version control and editor noise.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
